-- title:
--   Special-fibre Poincaré bundle at reductions of point divisors
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \geq 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a cyclotomic field $L = \mathbb{Q}(\zeta)$ for a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta$, the intermediate field $K$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$, a discrete valuation ring $A$ with fraction field $L$ whose maximal ideal contains $p$ and whose image contains $\zeta$, and $j \in K$, nonzero, whose Laurent expansion is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, let $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) with its structure morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, assumed proper, and let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $f$. Let $D$ be a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation for $f$ (a scheme over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ with a zero section), with $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ smooth and separated, together with: a witness `hrep` that $D$ represents rigidified line bundles on $X$ that are fibrewise algebraically equivalent to zero, a corresponding witness `hreps` for the base change of $f$ and of $\varepsilon$ to $k$ with designation $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\ k$, and an isomorphism `hPk` of the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` with the $k$-base change of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some` along the first projection of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ against $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $G$ be a [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9) (an abelian group $G.J0s$ with a distinguished subgroup and a surjection onto a product of two abelian groups with that subgroup as kernel) together with a bijection `pts` of $G.J0s$ with the $k$-points of $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\ k).\mathrm{toBase}$, and let $U$ be an open of $X$ which is smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and contains every such open. Finally let $Pl$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit, $\rho : A \to Pl$ compatible with the structure map $A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and $\pi_k : Pl \to k$ surjective with $\pi_k \circ \rho$ the structure map $A \to k$. The assertion is: for all $Pl$-points $\xi_1,\xi_2$ of $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} \rho$ whose topological images lie in $U$, all $k$-points $u_1,u_2$ of the base change $X_k$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ that reduce them (i.e. $u_i$ followed by the projection $X_k \to X$ equals $\operatorname{Spec} \pi_k$ followed by $\xi_i$), every $Pl$-point $s$ of $D$ over $\operatorname{Spec} \rho$ for which the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some` along $s$ is isomorphic to the dual of the ideal module of $\mathcal{O}(\xi_1)$ tensored with the ideal module of $\mathcal{O}(\xi_2)$ — where $\mathcal{O}(\xi)$ denotes the relative effective Cartier divisor `RelEffCartierDiv.ofPoint` cut out by the graph of $\xi$ — and every $y \in G.J0s$ whose associated $k$-point reduces $s$, one has an isomorphism of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` along `pts y` with the dual of the ideal module of $\mathcal{O}(u_1)$ tensored with the ideal module of $\mathcal{O}(u_2)$, and both ideal sheaves $\mathcal{O}(u_1)$, $\mathcal{O}(u_2)$ are invertible in the sense that locally they are generated by a single non-zero-divisor on affine basic opens.
--
--   This is the special-fibre half of the comparison between Abel–Jacobi classes on the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring and on its geometric special fibre: a divisor class $\mathcal{O}(\xi_1) - \mathcal{O}(\xi_2)$ supported in the smooth locus is read, after reduction, as $\mathcal{O}(u_1) - \mathcal{O}(u_2)$ on the fibre, with both point ideals invertible there. It is used by the results computing the two components of the projection $G.J0s \to J_I \times J_E$ on such classes.
